  "convention": "A speaker's roles are the entries official rosters print for them, and nothing else. `as` is the roster's own words, verbatim from the page at `url`: the White House list's lead-in, the Supreme Court list's section heading, the Biographical Directory's descriptor, the Senate state list's name. A speaker has one entry per roster section or page that lists them, and an empty list when no roster does. bioguide.congress.gov answers scripts with a bot challenge, so the Biographical Directory is read from the House's History, Art & Archives copy, which lists Representatives and Continental Congress delegates; Senate service comes from the Senate's own state lists. `bodies` are speakers that are not people. Transcribed once, on the accessed dates.",
